  "version": "zka:registry:v1",
  "description": "Canonical ZKA asset registry. Asset ids are CAIP-19-style `<chainId>/<assetNamespace>:<assetReference>` strings; per-chain encodings define how an asset projects into the in-circuit asset id / asset_commitment domain. Adapters fail closed on assets not registered for their chain.",
  "encodings": {
    "l1-erc20-keccak248": {
      "description": "ADR 0003 L1-anchored asset id: digest = keccak256(abi.encode(uint256(chainId), address(token))); the in-circuit field form is the digest with its top byte zeroed (value < 2^248), big-endian, which embeds as the identical integer in both BN254 and BLS12-377. Canonical reference implementation: src/zka-crypto/src/bridge.rs."
    }
  },
